          %p
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
          %p
            This book lays the basis of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+algebra"} categorical algebra
            – the study of the trinity
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            – in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebraic+theory"} (∞,1)-algebras
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-monad"} (∞,1)-monad
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} (∞,1)-operad
          %p
            In particular it discusses the analogs of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+%E2%88%9E-groups"} abelian ∞-groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            and
